    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d240">

                <pb facs="0354" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 818.00/34T</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Limon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-27T12:00:00-05:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1918, noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Gomez and Mariano Guardia, Minister of Finance under Gonzalez, and 60 men forced
                    to surrender at Turrialba by placing in front of Government lines two daughters
                    of Guardia. This stratagem boasted of by Tinoco commander, a cousin. Movement
                    practically over. Am encouraging ex-President Duran and members of Central
                    American Court of Justice to urge strongly retirement of Tinoco. Attitude of
                    latter is one of defiance of the United States. He has stated repeatedly that
                    for the honor of the country he will not get out at the suggestion of foreign
                    government, when real reason is simply desire for office and graft, and doubtful
                    as ever that he will voluntarily resign. Treatment to be given rebels still in
                    doubt. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
